// =============================================================================
// SaaS platform Prisma fragment: FeatureWithdrawal
// =============================================================================
//
// REFERENCE SNIPPET — see 01-subscription.prisma for conventions.
//
// One row per feature withdrawn for a reason outside the platform: an external
// service the feature depends on stopped, or a law took it away or changed it.
// From `effectiveFrom` the platform grants the feature to nobody, until the
// operator lifts the withdrawal from `liftedFrom`. Kept as evidence of what was
// announced, why, when and by whom, and of the reductions the operator named.
//
// What it means for each subscription it reaches — which lines, what each is
// reduced by — is a `subscription_notices` row of kind feature-withdrawn,
// written in the same transaction: its subject is this row's id.
//
// `reductions` is a JSON list of `{ kind, key, billingCycle, amountNet }`: the
// net amount a plan or an add-on, by its key, is reduced by for one whole
// period of that rhythm without the feature.
//
// At most ONE withdrawal of a feature is not lifted at a time. Prisma cannot
// express a partial unique index; the one that holds it is in
// sql/constraints.postgres.sql, and it is what makes two operators announcing
// at the same moment land one withdrawal rather than two.
//
// Optional: adopt it where an operator may withdraw features. Without it,
// withdrawing a feature is off.
//
// Contract: @saasicat/core (FeatureWithdrawalRepository).

model FeatureWithdrawal {
    id         String    @id @default(uuid())
    featureKey String
    // Why, in the operator's words, shown to the subscribers as written.
    reason     String

    effectiveFrom DateTime
    // Null until the operator lifts it.
    liftedFrom    DateTime?

    reductions Json @default("[]")

    announcedAt DateTime @default(now())
    // Who announced it, and who lifted it — actor tags, as the audit log writes them.
    announcedBy String
    liftedAt    DateTime?
    liftedBy    String?

    @@index([featureKey])
    @@map("feature_withdrawals")
}
